hadiths[47]{hadithnumber,text}:
"104","´It is narrated from Mus'ab bin Sa'd that` Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) came to visit Ibn 'Amir because Ibn 'Amir was ill. Ibn 'Amir said, ""O Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), will you not pray for me?"" He said, ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor does He accept charity from the spoils of war that is taken before its distribution. And you have been the governor of Basra."""
"105","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When any one of you wakes up from sleep, he should wash his hand three times before putting it into the vessel, because he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"106","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Avoid the two acts that bring curses (i.e., those because of which people curse you). The people asked: What are the two acts that bring curses? He (peace be upon him) said: One is relieving oneself on the road (where people pass by), and the other is relieving oneself in a shaded place (where people sit and rest). (Both of these acts cause harm to people, and they will speak ill and curse.)"
"107","‘Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Ja’far (may Allah be pleased with him) says that once the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) made me ride behind him on his mount, then he said something in my ear which I will not relate to anyone, and he liked to take cover behind a mound or date-palm trees at the time of relieving himself (so that no one could see his private parts). Ibn Asma’ in one narration said “wall of date-palms” instead of “grove of date-palms”."
"108","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would enter the toilet, he would say: ""O Allah! I seek refuge with You from male and female devils, or from filth, or impurities, or from devils and sins."""
"109","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him): The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you go to the toilet, do not face the Qiblah nor turn your back towards it while urinating or defecating, but rather turn your face towards the east or the west. (This refers to those regions where the Qiblah is towards the north or south. For those whose Qiblah is towards the east or west, they should turn their faces towards the north or south instead of the east or west.) Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Then we came to the land of Syria and saw that the latrines (toilets) were built facing the Qiblah, so we would turn our faces away from them and seek forgiveness from Allah Almighty."
"110","Wasih bin Haban says: I was praying in the mosque and Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) was sitting with his back towards the Qiblah. When I finished the prayer, I turned towards him from one side. Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: People say that when you sit to relieve yourself, do not face the Qiblah or Bayt al-Maqdis. (Once) I climbed onto the roof and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sitting for relieving himself facing Bayt al-Maqdis on two bricks (i.e., when facing Bayt al-Maqdis, his back would be towards the Qiblah)."
"111","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: None of you should urinate in standing water (and also do not do this: that after urinating) then perform ghusl (ritual bath) with that water. In another narration, it is stated: Do not do this, that you urinate in standing water which does not flow, and then perform ghusl with that same water."
"112","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by two graves and said: ""These two are being punished, and not for something major. One of them used to carry tales (i.e., spread gossip to cause discord), and the other did not take care to protect himself from urine."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked for a fresh date-palm branch, split it into two, and placed one piece on each grave. He said: ""Perhaps their punishment will be lightened as long as these branches do not dry."""
"113","'Abdullah bin Abi Qatadah narrates from his father (Abu Qatadah) (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: None of you should hold his private part with his right hand while urinating, nor should he clean himself after defecation with his right hand, nor should he blow into a vessel."
"114","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, entered a garden and a boy followed behind him. He had a water vessel with him, and that boy was the youngest among us. He placed the vessel near a berry tree, and then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, relieved himself, performed istinja (cleaning) with water, and then came out."
"115","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: When any of you cleans the place of excretion with stones, he should clean it with an odd number of stones, and when any of you performs ablution, he should put water into his nose and then blow it out."
"116","Saidna Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) says that he was asked, ""Did your Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) teach you everything, even the matters of defecation and urination?"" He replied, ""Yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade us from facing the Qiblah while urinating or defecating, and also forbade us from cleaning ourselves with the right hand, or with less than three stones, or with dung or bones."""
"117","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) says that` a slave woman of Umm al-Mu'mineen Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) was given a goat in charity, and it died. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw it lying there and said: Why did you not remove its skin? You could have tanned it and used it. So the people said: O Messenger of Allah! It was dead. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eating the dead animal is forbidden."
"118","It is narrated from Yazid bin Abi Habib that Abu'l-Khair told him: I saw Ibn Wahla al-Saba'i wearing a fur coat. I touched it, and he said: Ibn Wahla, why are you touching it (do you consider it impure)? I said to Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): We live in the land of the Maghreb, where there are many Berber disbelievers and fire-worshippers. They bring slaughtered rams to us. We do not eat the animals they slaughter, and they bring skins filled with fat. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: The skin becomes pure by tanning (i.e., the skin becomes pure by tanning, even if a disbeliever has tanned it)."
"119","‘Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughaffal (may Allah be pleased with him) says that’ the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered the killing of dogs. Then he said, “What is the matter with these people and dogs?” Then he permitted keeping dogs for hunting and for the protection of livestock (that is, for the protection of goats), and said, “When a dog drinks from a vessel by putting its mouth in it, wash it seven times and scrub it with earth the eighth time.” And in the narration of Yahya bin Sa‘id, it is mentioned that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) permitted keeping dogs for hunting, for goats, and for the protection of crops."
"120","Sayyiduna Abu Malik Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Purity is half of faith, and ""Alhamdulillah"" fills the scale (i.e., its reward is so great that it fills the scale of deeds), and ""Subhanallah"" and ""Alhamdulillah"" together fill the space between the heavens and the earth. Prayer is light, charity is proof, patience is illumination, and the Qur'an will be an argument for you or against you (if you act upon the Qur'an, it will be an argument in your favor, otherwise it will be a burden against you). Every person (whether good or bad) sets out in the morning and either frees himself (from Allah's punishment by doing good deeds) or destroys himself (by doing bad deeds)."
"121","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a servant, a Muslim or a believer (the narrator is unsure), performs ablution and washes his face, all the (minor) sins committed by his eyes come out from his face with the water or with the last drop of water (the narrator is also unsure about this). Then when he washes his hands, every sin committed by his hands comes out from his hands with the water or with the last drop of water. Then when he washes his feet, every sin which he committed by walking with his feet comes out with the water or with the last drop of water, until he emerges purified from all sins."
"122","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he spent a night with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). In the latter part of the night, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) got up, went outside, and looked towards the sky. Then he recited this verse which is in Surah Al-Imran: ((Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of the night...)) up to ((So protect us from the punishment of the Fire)). Then he returned inside, used the miswak, performed ablution, and stood to pray. Then he lay down, then got up, went outside, looked towards the sky, and recited the same verse. Then he returned inside, used the miswak, performed ablution, and again stood to pray."
"123","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa Tayyiba Tahira (may Allah be pleased with her) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the house, he would first use the miswak."
"124","‘It is narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa Tayyiba Tahira (may Allah be pleased with her) that’ indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked to begin with the right side in purification, combing his hair, and putting on his shoes."
"125","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd bin Asim Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, and he was a companion, that people said to him, ""Show us how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution."" So he called for a vessel (of water), tilted it, and first poured water over both his hands. (From this, it is understood that at the beginning of ablution, it is recommended to wash both hands including the fingers, before putting the hands into the water.) And he washed them three times. Then he put his hand into the vessel and took it out, and with a single handful rinsed his mouth and put water into his nose. Then he did the same three times. Then he put his hand in and took it out and washed his face three times. (In the narration of Bukhari, it is mentioned that he joined both hands together to take water and washed his face three times.) Then he put his hand into the vessel and took it out and washed both his hands up to the elbows twice each. Then he put his hand into the vessel and took it out and wiped his head, first moving both hands from the front to the back, then from the back to the front (i.e., returning to the forehead). Then he washed both feet including the ankles. After that, he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution in this manner."
"126","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Whoever performs ablution should put water into his nose and then expel it. It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: When any one of you wakes up from sleep, he should expel water from his nose three times, for indeed Satan spends the night at the tip of the nose or in the middle veins of the nose."
"127","Narrated from Naeem bin Abdullah Mujmir that: I saw Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) performing ablution; when he washed his face, he washed it thoroughly. Then he washed his right hand up to and including a part of his upper arm. Then he washed his left hand up to and including a part of his upper arm. Then he wiped his head. Then he washed his right foot, including a part of his shin. Then he washed his left foot up to and including a part of his shin. Then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performing ablution in this manner, and he said: On the Day of Resurrection, your foreheads and hands and feet will be shining white (radiant) because of the traces of ablution. Therefore, whoever among you wishes to increase his brightness, let him do so (i.e., let him wash his limbs thoroughly and up to farther parts)."
"128","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to the graveyard and said, “Peace be upon you, O abode of the Muslims, and if Allah wills, we shall join you. I wish that we could see our brothers.” (From this hadith it is known that it is permissible to wish for good things, such as meeting scholars and virtuous people.) The noble Companions (may Allah be pleased with them all) said, “O Messenger of Allah! Are we not your brothers?” He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “You are my companions, and our brothers are those who have not yet come into the world.” The Companions said, “O Messenger of Allah! How will you recognize those people of your ummah whom you have not seen?” He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Suppose among you someone has a horse with a white forehead and white legs among black horses, will he not recognize his horse?” The Companions said, “Indeed, he will recognize it.” He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “On the Day of Resurrection, my ummah will have radiant faces and radiant hands and feet because of ablution, and I will precede them at the Hawd (Pond) of Kawthar. Beware! Some people will be driven away from my Hawd just as a stray camel is driven away. I will call them, ‘Come, come!’ At that time it will be said, ‘These people changed (their ways) after you (or their condition changed, they became involved in innovation and oppression).’ Then I will say, ‘Go away, go away.’”"
"129","It is narrated from Humran, who was the freed slave of Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) called for water for ablution and performed ablution. First, he washed both hands up to the wrists three times, then rinsed his mouth and put water into his nose. Then he washed his face three times, then washed his right hand up to the elbow, then washed his left hand three times, then wiped his head. Then he washed his right foot three times, then washed his left foot three times. After that, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution in the same way as I have just performed ablution. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution like my ablution, then stands and prays two rak‘ahs, not letting his mind wander to anything else during them, his previous sins will be forgiven. Ibn Shihab said: Our scholars used to say that this ablution is the most complete of all ablutions performed for prayer."
"130","It is narrated from Humran that Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution completely as Allah Almighty has commanded him, then the obligatory prayers will be an expiation for all the sins committed between those prayers."
"131","Narrated from Sayyiduna Uthman (bin Affan) (may Allah be pleased with him): He said that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever performs ablution perfectly for prayer, then goes to the (mosque) for the obligatory prayer and prays with the people or in congregation or in the mosque, Allah Almighty will forgive his sins."
"132","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not tell you about those things by which sins are erased (i.e., forgiven or wiped out from the record of the scribes) and ranks are elevated (in Paradise)? The people said: Why not, O Messenger of Allah! Please tell us. He (peace be upon him) said: Performing ablution thoroughly (properly) even in difficulty (such as severe cold or illness), and taking many steps towards the mosques (such that the house is far from the mosque and one goes repeatedly), and waiting for one prayer after another prayer. That is ribat (i.e., restraining the soul for worship)."
"133","Abu Hazim narrates: I was behind Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he was performing ablution for prayer and was washing his hand so far up that he washed up to his armpit. I said, ""O Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), what kind of ablution is this?"" He said, ""O descendants of Farukh (Farukh is the name of a son of Ibrahim, peace be upon him, whose descendants are among the non-Arabs, and Abu Hazim was also non-Arab), are you present here? If I had known you were present here, I would not have performed ablution in this manner. I heard my friend (the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him) say, 'On the Day of Resurrection, a believer will be adorned with jewelry up to the place where his ablution reaches.'"""
"134","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) told me that a man performed ablution and left a spot on his foot, the size of a fingernail, dry. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw him and said, ""Go and perform ablution properly."" So he went back, then returned and offered prayer."
"135","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform ablution with one mudd and would perform ghusl with one saa’ up to five mudd. (One saa’ is two and a half kilograms and a “mudd” is a quarter of a saa’.)"
"136","It is narrated from Hammam that Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) urinated, then performed ablution and wiped over his socks. The people said, ""Do you do this?"" He replied, ""Yes, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) urinate, then perform ablution and wipe over both his socks."" A’mash said that Ibrahim said, ""This hadith was very pleasing to the people because Jarir became Muslim after Surah Al-Ma'idah (in which washing the feet in ablution is mentioned) was revealed."""
"137","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Wa'il (may Allah be pleased with him) that Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) was extremely strict regarding the matter of urine, to the extent that he used to urinate in a bottle and would say that among the Children of Israel, when urine touched anyone's body, he would cut off the skin (with scissors). Sayyiduna Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) said that I wish Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) would not have been so strict, for I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he came to a garbage dump (i.e., a place for rubbish), and stood behind a wall just as any one of you stands, then urinated. I moved away, but he signaled to me to come closer, so I stood by his heels until he finished urinating. In another narration, it is added that then he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."
"138","Narrated from Sayyiduna Mughirah bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him): I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on a journey. He asked, “Do you have water with you?” I said, “Yes, I do.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) dismounted from his ride and walked away until he disappeared from sight in the dark night. Then he returned, and I poured water for him from a bucket. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) washed his face. He was wearing a woolen cloak, and it was difficult for him to bring his hands out through the sleeves, so he brought his hands out from underneath and washed them, and wiped over his head. Then, when I bent down to remove his leather socks, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Leave them. I put them on in a state of purity,” and he wiped over both of them."
"139","Shuraih bin Hani narrates: I came to Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) to ask her about wiping over the socks, so she said: ""Ask the son of Abu Talib (that is, Ali, may Allah be pleased with him), for he used to travel with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."" We asked him, and he said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prescribed the duration of wiping for a traveler as three days and three nights, and for a resident as one day and one night."""
"140","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Mughirah bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed behind during a journey, and I also stayed behind with him. When the Prophet (peace be upon him) finished relieving himself, he asked, “Do you have any water?” So I brought a vessel of water. The Prophet (peace be upon him) washed his hands and face. Then, when he wanted to take his arms out of his sleeves, the sleeves became tight (i.e., he could not take them out), so the Prophet (peace be upon him) took his hand out from below and placed the cloak on his shoulders, and washed both hands, and wiped over his forehead, turban, and leather socks. Then he mounted (his ride), and I also mounted. When we reached our people, they were praying. Sayyiduna ‘Abdur Rahman bin ‘Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) was leading them in prayer, and he had already performed one rak‘ah. When he realized that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) had arrived, he began to move back. The Prophet (peace be upon him) gestured to him to remain in his place. So he led the prayer. When he finished with the salam, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) stood up, and I also stood up, and we performed the rak‘ah that we had missed before."
"141","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) wiped over the socks and the turban."
"142","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Buraidah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed several prayers with one ablution on the day of the conquest of Makkah and wiped over his socks. Sayyiduna Umar Farooq (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Today you have done something which you have never done before."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied, ""I have done this intentionally."""
"143","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) that we used to herd camels. When it was my turn, I brought the camels back in the evening to their resting place and saw that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was standing and giving admonition to the people. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever among the Muslims performs ablution well, then stands and offers two rak‘ahs, focusing his heart and face (i.e., being attentive both outwardly and inwardly, neither letting his heart be distracted by worldly thoughts nor turning his face here and there), Paradise will become obligatory for him. I said, “How excellent is the statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) (for such a great reward with so little effort)!” At this, someone in front of me said, “The first statement was even better than this.” I looked carefully and saw that it was Sayyiduna Umar Farooq (may Allah be pleased with him). He said, “I saw that you have just arrived. (So listen to this as well:) The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever among you performs ablution well and completely, then says (translation): ‘I bear witness that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, and Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is His servant and Messenger,’ for him the eight gates of Paradise will be opened, and he may enter through whichever gate he wishes.”"
"144","`Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I was a man who had a lot of madhiy (pre-seminal fluid), and I felt shy to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because his daughter was married to me, so I asked Sayyiduna Miqdad bin Aswad (may Allah be pleased with him) to ask (on my behalf). He asked, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He should wash his private part and perform wudu (ablution)."
"145","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that (on one occasion) the iqamah for prayer was pronounced and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was conversing in private with a man. The wording of Abdul Warith’s narration is that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was conversing in private with a man, and he did not stand up for the prayer until the people (while sitting) fell asleep. And in the narration of Shu’bah, it is mentioned that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained engaged in private conversation until the Companions (while sitting) fell asleep. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and led them in prayer (and did not instruct them to perform a new ablution)."
"146","Narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), ""Should I perform ablution after eating goat meat?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""If you wish, perform ablution, and if you wish, do not."" Then he asked, ""Should I perform ablution after eating camel meat?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Yes! Perform ablution after eating camel meat."" He asked, ""Should I pray in sheep pens?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Yes."" He asked, ""Should I pray in camel enclosures?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""No."""
"147","It is narrated from 'Umar bin Abdul Aziz that 'Abdullah bin Ibrahim bin Qariz informed him that he saw Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) performing ablution in the mosque. He said: I have eaten pieces of cheese, so I am performing ablution, because I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Perform ablution after eating anything that has been cooked over fire."
"148","Ja'far bin Amr bin Umayyah al-Damri narrates from his father, Sayyiduna Amr bin Umayyah al-Damri (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) cutting and eating the shoulder of a goat with a knife. In the meantime, he was called for prayer, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) put down the knife, performed the prayer, and did not perform ablution."
"149","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) drank milk. Then he asked for water, rinsed his mouth, and said: ""Milk makes the mouth greasy."""
"150","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When any one of you feels a disturbance in his stomach during prayer, and he is unsure whether anything has come out of him or not, that is, whether wind has been passed or not, he should not leave the mosque until he hears a sound or perceives a smell (i.e., until he is certain that he has broken his wudu)."
